o be sure.\n\nLet me also handle `ext` and `ins`:\n- EXT rd, rs, pos, size: opcode SPECIAL3 (0x1f), funct 0x00. pos=(instr>>6)&0x1f (bits 10-6), size=(instr>>11)&0x1f (bits 15-11) + 1 (size field is size-1). rd = (instr>>11)... wait. EXT format: rd (bits 15-11), rs (bits 25-21), pos (bits 10-6), size (bits 5-0)? Let me recall. \n\n  EXT rd, rs, pos, size:\n  - opcode = SPECIAL3 (0x1f)\n  - rs (bits 25-21): source register\n  - rt (bits 20-16): dest register (rd, but in rt field)\n  - msbd (bits 15-11): size-1\n  - lsb (bits 10-6): pos\n  - funct (bits 5-0): 0x00 (EXT)\n  \n  So: rs=(instr>>21)&0x1f, rt=(instr>>16)&0x1f (dest), pos=(instr>>6)&0x1f, size=((instr>>11)&0x1f)+1. result = (gpr[rs] >>> pos) & ((1<<size)-1). gpr[rt] = result.\n\n- INS rd, rs, pos, size:\n  - opcode SPECIAL3 (0x1f), funct 0x04.\n  - rs (25-21), rt (20-16) dest, msb (15-11), lsb (10-6), funct 0x04.\n  - pos = lsb = (instr>>6)&0x1f, msb = (instr>>11)&0x1f, size = msb - lsb + 1.\n  - result = (gpr[rt] & ~mask) | ((gpr[rs] & ((1<<size)-1)) << pos). where mask = ((1<<size)-1) << pos.\n\n- BSHFL (SPECIAL3 funct 0x20): the sa field (bits 10-6) determines:\n  - 0x02 WSBH: swap bytes within each halfword. rd = (instr>>11)&0x1f, rt=(instr>>16)&0x1f.\n  - 0x10 SEB: sign-extend byte. rd = sext8(gpr[rt] & 0xff).\n  - 0x18 SEH: sign-extend halfword. rd = sext16(gpr[rt] & 0xffff).\n  - 0x03 SHFL? no.\n\nLet me verify seb/seh/wsbh encodings from disasm. The disasm showed `seh` (31), `seb` (17), `wsbh` (6), `nor` (17).\n\nOK I think I have enough. Let me also handle `movn`/`movz`:\n- MOVN rd, rs, rt (SPECIAL funct 0x0b): if gpr[rt]!=0, gpr[rd]=gpr[rs].\n- MOVZ rd, rs, rt (0x0a): if gpr[rt]==0, gpr[rd]=gpr[rs].\n\nAnd the conditional moves MOVT/MOVF for FP (covered above).\n\nNow, let me also double-check the `ror` and a few encodings by disassembling specific ones. Let me grab a few ror, ext, ins, wsbh, seb, seh instructions.\n\nActually, let me just write the interpreter with all these and test it. If somet